  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-b/q3",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q3-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The manager of a cinema believes that the weights, X grams, of popcorn bags sold in his cinema are Normally distributed with mean of 340 and standard deviation of 10. a) Taking µ = 340 and σ = 10 ... i. ... find, to the nearest gram, the weight 0x exceeded by 5% of these popcorn bags. ( ) 4 ii. ... ( P X &gt; µ X &lt; x ) . ( ) 2 0 A new manager, which takes over the cinema, asks his staff to investigate the weights of these popcorn bags and is told that it was subsequently found that µ = 320 and σ = 10 .\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q3-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The new manager claims that µ has to be higher than 320, as the mean of a random sample of 5 bags was found to be 327 . b) Using σ = 10 , conduct a hypothesis test at the 5% level of significance to investigate the new manager&#x27;s claim. State your hypotheses clearly. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q3-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) With X ∼N(340, 102), (i) P(X &gt; x0) = 0.05, [B1] hence P(X &lt; x0) = 1 −0.05 . = 0.95 Standardising gives P(Z &lt; (x0 −340)/10) = 0.95, so (x0 −340)/10 = Φ−1(0.95) ≈1.64485. [M1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q3-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"This gives x0 = 340 + 10(1.64485 . . .) , [A1] = 356.4485 . . . or 356 g to the nearest gram: [A1] (ii) The area below the unrounded x0 is 0.95, and the area between µ and x0 is 0.95 −0.50 = 0.45. [B1] Therefore P(X &gt; µ | X &lt; x0) = 0.45 0.95 [A1] 9 = 19 ≈0.4737.\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q3-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"(b) Setting up the hypothesis: Let µ be the population mean bag weight: Test H0 : µ = 320 against H1 : µ &gt; 320. [B1] The sample gives n = 5, ¯x = 327 and the population standard deviation is 10. At the 5% level, the upper-tail critical value is Φ−1(0.95) = 1.6449. [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q3-solution-4.svg\" alt=\"√ The null standard error is 10/ 5. [A1] Use z = (¯x −µ0)/(σ/√n).\" style=\"--madas-width:426.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q3-solution-5.svg\" alt=\"Thus √ z = (327 −320)/(10/ 5) . [A1] = 1.5652 Since 1.5652 &lt; 1.6449, retain H0. [A1] There is insufficient evidence that the mean weight exceeds 320 g . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:645.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 3 is 12 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "The manager of a cinema believes that the weights, X grams, of popcorn bags sold in his cinema are Normally distributed with mean of 340 and standard deviation of 10. a) Taking µ = 340 and σ = 10 ... i. ... find, to the nearest gram, the weight 0x exceeded by 5% of these popcorn bags. ( ) 4 ii. ... ( P X > µ X < x ) . ( ) 2 0 A new manager, which takes over the cinema, asks his staff to investigate the weights of these popcorn bags and is told that it was subsequently found that µ = 320 and σ = 10 . The new manager claims that µ has to be higher than 320, as the mean of a random sample of 5 bags was found to be 327 . b) Using σ = 10 , conduct a hypothesis test at the 5% level of significance to investigate the new manager's claim. State your hypotheses clearly. ( ) 6"
  },
