    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-b/q4",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q4-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Frequency Density 2 1.5 1 0.5 0 4.5 8.5 12.5 14.5 16.5 20.5 0 height\" style=\"--madas-width:500.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q4-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The histogram above shows the distribution of the heights, to the nearest cm, of some plants in a garden centre. It is further given that there were 18 plants with a height between 5 cm and 8 cm, rounded to the nearest cm. a) Use the histogram to estimate the median. ( ) 6 b) Estimate, by calculation, the mean and the standard deviation of the heights of these plants. ( ) 6\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q4-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Heights rounded to 5–8 cm have class boundaries 4.5 ≤h &lt; 8.5. The first bar has width 4 and height 0.3, so an area of 1.2 represents 18 plants: Each unit of area represents 15 plants:\" style=\"--madas-width:509.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q4-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(a) The bar areas are 0.3(4), 1.2(4), 2(2), 1.6(2), 0.8(4). Thus the areas of the five bars are 1.2, 4.8, 4, 3.2, 3.2, for a total of 16.4. [M1] The median splits the area at 8.2. [A1] The area to the left of 12.5 is 6.0, so go a further (8.2 −6.0)/2 = 1.1 [A1] into the third bar: [A1] The median is 12.5 + 1.1, approximately 13.6 cm . [M1] [A1] (b) Using the class midpoints x gives the following grouped data: Height (rounded, cm) 5–8 9–12 13–14 15–16 17–20 Midpoint x 6.5 10.5 13.5 15.5 18.5 Bar area 1.2 4.8 4.0 3.2 3.2 Frequency f = 15 × area 18 72 60 48 48 [A1] The midpoints are the averages of the class endpoints: Multiply each midpoint by its frequency to form fx, and its square by its frequency to form fx2.\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q4-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"The totals are P f = 246, [A1] P fx = 3315 [A1] and P fx2 = 47593.5. [A1] The estimated mean is 3315/246 ≈13.48 cm , [A1] and the estimated standard deviation is s 47593.5 3315 2 − ≈3.45 cm . [A1] 246 246\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 4 is 12 marks.</p>"
