  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-b/q7",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A car of mass 1500 kg is towing a trailer of mass 500 kg by means of a light rigid horizontal towbar. The car is experiencing a constant air resistance of 300 N , while the corresponding constant air resistance on the trailer is 100 N . The car and trailer are modelled as particles. a) Given the tension in the towbar is 200 N ,  calculate … i. … the acceleration of the system. ( ) 3 ii. … the driving force of the car. ( ) 3 Later in the journey, the car’s driving force is removed and the car’s brakes are applied, providing a constant breaking force of 400 N , on the car only.\" style=\"--madas-width:588.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q7-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The air resistance on the car and trailer are unchanged. b) Determine … i. … the deceleration of the system. ( ) 3 ii. … the thrust in the towbar. ( ) 3\" style=\"--madas-width:588.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Worked solution diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:536.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Take the direction of travel as positive: Let D represent the driving force. (a) With the towbar in tension, the force on the trailer from the towbar is forwards: (i) Use the trailer alone: 200 −100 = 500a, [M1] so 100 = 500a, giving a = 0.2 m s−2 . [M1] [A1] (ii) For the car alone, D −300 −200 = 1500a, so D −500 = 1500(0.2) = 300, giving D = 800. For the combined system, D −300 −100 = 2000(0.2), [M1] so D = 800 N . [M1] [A1] (b) The engine force is removed and the brakes act on the car: (i) Keep the original tension arrows and let S be signed tension: The trailer gives S −100 = 500a and the car gives −300 −S −400 = 1500a. Adding eliminates S.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q7-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"For the combined system, −400 −300 −100 = 2000a. [M1] This gives a = −0.4 m s−2, [A1] a deceleration of 0.4 m s−2 . [A1] (ii) Substituting into the trailer equation gives S −100 = 500(−0.4) = −200, so S = −100 N. The negative tension is a thrust: The towbar pushes backwards on the trailer: [B1] If the thrust is T, then −T −100 = 500(−0.4), [A1] so T = 100 N . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 12 marks.</p>"
    ],
    "promptText": "A car of mass 1500 kg is towing a trailer of mass 500 kg by means of a light rigid horizontal towbar. The car is experiencing a constant air resistance of 300 N , while the corresponding constant air resistance on the trailer is 100 N . The car and trailer are modelled as particles. a) Given the tension in the towbar is 200 N ,  calculate … i. … the acceleration of the system. ( ) 3 ii. … the driving force of the car. ( ) 3 Later in the journey, the car’s driving force is removed and the car’s brakes are applied, providing a constant breaking force of 400 N , on the car only. The air resistance on the car and trailer are unchanged. b) Determine … i. … the deceleration of the system. ( ) 3 ii. … the thrust in the towbar. ( ) 3"
  },
  {
    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-b/q8",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q8-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Relative to a fixed origin O , the horizontal unit vectors i and j are pointing due east and due north, respectively. Two helicopters, P and Q , are flying with constant velocities in the same horizontal plane. At noon, P is at the point with position vector ( 20 i + 35 j km . The position ) vector of P at time t hours after noon is p . 1 a) Given that when t = hours, p = ( 65 i + 59 j km , determine the velocity of P . ) 2 ( ) 3 b) Find an expression for p , in terms of t . ( ) 2 At noon, Q is at the point with position vector 200j km .\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q8-question-2.svg\" alt=\"The speed of  Q is 125 kmh−, in the direction ( 1 ) 24 i − 7 j . The position vector of  Q , at time t hours after noon, is q . c) Find an expression for q , in terms of t . ( ) 4 d) Calculate the distance between P and Q when t = 2 . ( ) 4\" style=\"--madas-width:580.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-b/q8-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) Use r = r0 + tv. Thus 65i + 59j = 20i + 35j + 1 2v, so 1 2v = 45i + 24j. Over half an hour P moves 45i + 24j km, so its velocity is (90i + 48j) km h−1 . [M1] [M1] [A1] (b) Use p = (20i + 35j) + (90i + 48j)t. Add the displacement to the initial position: p = (20 + 90t)i + (35 + 48t)j . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
